            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0380" n="278" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg278"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4/2244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-10-17T19:00:00-05:00">October 17, 1933—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>131. Your 170, October 17, 11 a.m.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d216-f1"/> Department’s
                    October 14, 10 a.m., was sent to countries adjacent to Germany asking for an
                    analysis of the situation growing out of Germany’s withdrawal from the League
                    and the Disarmament Conference. We shall hope soon for your analysis of the
                    situation in Germany from both internal and international angles.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
